// Writes the golden fixtures from the frozen TypeScript game (ADR 0030, T84.2) into
// `crates/csp-sim/fixtures/`; the Rust port is judged against them. Deterministic: two runs write
// the same bytes. Nothing it writes is edited by hand.
//
// Usage, from the repo root:
//   corepack pnpm exec tsx --conditions=source scripts/dump-fixtures.mts [--full] [--db <path>]
//     --full        also hashes the full-size map (`terrain/1-<MAP_SIZE>.sha256`); takes minutes
//     --db <path>   a `world.db` to take the live save from (copied first, never written)
//     --out <dir>   where to write (default `crates/csp-sim/fixtures`)
//     --quick       small sizes and few ticks, for the script's own test
//     --only <parts>  only these, comma-separated: balance, random, terrain, lang, paths, save,
//                     worlds, generated, sight (default all); the README keeps every other file

